      "hint_steps": ["f(4) tells you the input x is 4.", "Replace x with 4: f(4)=2(4)+3.", "2(4)+3=8+3=11, so the answer is 11."],
      "solution_steps": [{"equation":"f(4)=2(4)+3","explanation":"Substitute 4 for x."},{"equation":"f(4)=8+3","explanation":"Multiply first."},{"equation":"f(4)=11","explanation":"Add to get the output."}],
      "alternate_solution_steps": [{"equation":"input 4 → rule 2x+3 → output 11","explanation":"Think of the function as a machine: put in 4, double it, then add 3."}],
      "tutor_behavior": "Identify the input inside the parentheses, substitute it for x, then simplify."
    },
    {
